class:: ClusterPMOsc
summary:: Four-operator PM network with additive-cluster operators
categories:: UGens>Generators>Deterministic
related:: Guides/NovelOscillators

description::

ClusterPMOsc is a four-operator phase-modulation network in which every
operator contains four sine components. Shared cluster ratios and amplitudes
define the local spectrum; the PM matrix defines how operator outputs interact.

The sixteen PM entries use row-major order. Entry
code::(row * 4) + column:: routes the preceding oversampled substep of operator
code::column:: into operator code::row::. Each local cluster removes
components at Nyquist with a smooth fade and normalizes by its active absolute
amplitude sum.

The closest vanilla UGen is link::Classes/Klang::. Both sum fixed-ratio sine
components, but ClusterPMOsc embeds four such sums in a feedback-capable PM
network with audio-rate matrix elements and optional oversampling.

classmethods::

method:: ar

argument:: freq
Signed network base frequency in hertz.

argument:: ratios
Exactly four operator-frequency ratios. Elements may be audio rate.

argument:: clusterRatios
Exactly four shared local component ratios, clamped to code::-64..64::.

argument:: clusterAmplitudes
Exactly four shared local component amplitudes, clamped to code::-8..8::.

argument:: pm
Exactly sixteen row-major PM coefficients in radians. Elements may be audio
rate.

argument:: amplitudes
Exactly four operator output amplitudes, clamped to code::-4..4::.

argument:: oversample
Initialization-rate value code::1::, code::2::, or code::4::.

argument:: mul
Multiplier applied to all four outputs.

argument:: add
Offset added to all four outputs after multiplication.

returns::
An array containing operators 0 through 3.

method:: kr

ClusterPMOsc is audio-rate only. This method throws an error.

subsection:: Discussion

A zero PM matrix produces four independent additive oscillators. A local
cluster whose only nonzero component is ratio one reduces to a sine operator.
Feedback always reads the preceding internal substep, which prevents
algebraic loops and makes repeated renders deterministic.

examples::

code::
(
{ ClusterPMOsc.ar(70)[0] * 0.075 }.play;
)
::

code::
(
{
    var pm = [
        0, 2, 0, 0,
        0, 0, 1, 0,
        0.5, 0, 0, 1,
        0, 0.3, 0, 0
    ];
    Splay.ar(
        ClusterPMOsc.ar(
            55, [1, 1.5, 2, 3],
            [1, 1.01, 2, 3],
            [1, 0.3, 0.15, 0.08],
            pm, [1, 0.4, 0.2, 0.1], 2
        )
    ) * 0.035;
}.play;
)
::

